><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This is the first study to showthat consuming A-LAC after a&#xD;simulated evening competition can improve both sleep characteristics,&#xD;together with physical and cognitive performance recovery.&#xD;The demonstrated increase in plasma Trp/LNAA after&#xD;A-LAC may also offer an insight into the mechanisms behind&#xD;the improved sleep characteristics that were observed. Based&#xD;on these findings, A-LAC supplementation could be used by&#xD;athletes to improve sleep and performance recovery after evening&#xD;training or competition. Consuming A-LAC after evening&#xD;exercise may be useful during competition situations that involve&#xD;short turnarounds between games, as well as congested&#xD;competition schedules. Based on these promising results, further&#xD;research on the efficacy of A-LAC supplementation&#xD;during situations that are known to impair athlete sleep, such as&#xD;travel and demanding competition schedules, should be&#xD;conducted.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="8" rect="584.956970,207.211670,768.956970,299.211670"
/></highlight
></annots
